ory":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids March to April and May to June each came in under 90% of normal in 40 of them. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, January to February ran 14% of normal and May to June ran 209%. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, with grid 17792 at 29%. Grid 18094 shows a preliminary July to August 2026 estimate of 42.2, figured from NOAA rain and not RMA&rsquo;s index.</p>"}
